SEC. 51P-781.114. ADDITIONAL PROVISIONS.

(a) The Property must be properly maintained in a state of good repair and neat appearance.

(b) Development and use of the property must comply with all federal and state laws and regulations, and with all ordinances, rules, and regulations of the city.

(c) Except as provided in this subsection, a shared access development must comply with Section 51A-4.411.

(1) No more than 41 individual lots may be platted as a shared access development.

(2) One shared access area may serve a maximum of 41 dwelling units.

(3) The two shared access points must be located on Emerald Isle Drive.

(d) At least 30 days before filing an application for a development plan, the Property owner must mail notices of the application by certified mail, return receipt requested, to the designated representative, as identified by the Department of Sustainable Development and Construction, of:

(1) The Peninsula Neighborhood Association;

(2) Forest Hills Association;

(3) Little Forest Hills Neighborhood Association;

(4) Casa Linda Estates Neighborhood Association;

(5) White Rock Neighborhood Association;

(6) Emerald Isle Neighborhood Association; and

(7) Save White Rock Lake. (Ord. 27135; 27737)
